Tidy←{
  ⍝ Tidy
  ⍝ Try to align comments nicely in dfn or tradfn source.
  ⍝ ---------
  ⍝ Syntax:
  ⍝ @cvv← [(tab: 65 ⋄ inc: 5  ⋄ min: 15  ⋄ pairs: 0 ⋄ fi: 0 )] ∇ [source | sourceFnOp | sourceFi]
  ⍝ ⍵:
  ⍝   source:      the source document to format.   @cvv: a char vector of vectors.
  ⍝   sourceFnOp:  the name of a function or operator with the code to format, with (fi:0).  @cv: a char vector.
  ⍝   sourceFi:    the name of a file with the code to format, with (fi:1). @cv: a char vector, (fi: 1).
  ⍝ ⍺:
  ⍝   tab:   column in which to put comments if possible.
  ⍝   inc:   If text extends to <tab> or beryond, place comments multiples of <inc>
  ⍝          to the right of position <tab>
  ⍝   min:   Keep any comments before column <min> where they are.
  ⍝   fi:    If 1 and ⍵ has depth ≤1, treats ⍵ as the name of a file to update in place (see below).
  ⍝          Otherwise, a char vector right arg is treated as a fn or operator name.
  ⍝   pairs: If 1, will recognize pairs of comments on line line, 
  ⍝            - the first a left-side comment and
  ⍝            - the other aligned with the right-hand side comments. 
  ⍝          - The two must be have at least 5 blanks in between. 
  ⍝          If 0, only one comment is allowed.
  ⍝ Example of pairs: 
  ⍝|   ⍝ this is the left-side comment                      ⍝ And this is the right-side comment
  ⍝|                                                        ⍝ This is only a right-side comment
  ⍝
  ⍝ Description
  ⍝ 1. If source is a char vector of vectors, it is treated as multiline APL code (a fn, op, etc.)
  ⍝    a.  Return the source with comments aligned per options.
  ⍝    b.  The object is NOT refixed-- that's up to you.
  ⍝ 2. If source is a char. vector, and...
  ⍝    a.  if fi is 0,
  ⍝        - ⍵ refers to the name of a visible function;
  ⍝        - its source representation (verbatim if possible) is formatted and...
  ⍝          - returned as a shy value;
  ⍝    b.  if fi is 1,
  ⍝        - ⍵ refers to a file, which is read;
  ⍝        - its source is formatted and...
  ⍝          - rewritten to the file (in place) and
  ⍝          - returned as a shy value.
  ⍝
  11 22::⎕SIGNAL⊂⎕DMX.('EN'EN ⋄ 'Message'Message)
      ⎕IO ⎕ML←0 1
      ⍺←()
      fnOpÊ←('EN' 11 ⋄ 'Message' 'Unknown function or operator')
      optÊ←('EN' 11 ⋄ 'Message' 'Unknown option(s)')
      ∆Tidy←∇                                               ⍝ Recurse Tidy
      opts←(                                                ⍝ Default options
        tab: 60 ⋄ inc: 5 ⋄ min: 20 ⋄ pairs: 0 ⋄ fi: 0 
      )
      FnOrFi←opts∘{
        ~⍺.fi:_←⍺{
            ~⍵ ⎕NC⍛∊3 4:⎕SIGNAL⊂fnOpÊ
              ⍺ ∆Tidy 62 ⎕ATX ⍵
        }⍵
            ⍺.fi←0
            ll←⍺ ∆Tidy⊃⎕NGET ⍵ 1
        1:_←ll⊣ll⊂⍛⎕NPUT ⍵ 1
      }
      Align←{(t i)p←⍺ ⍵ ⋄ p≤t:''⍴⍨t-p ⋄ ''⍴⍨i|p-t}

      ×≢⊃~/(⍺ opts).⎕NL ¯2:⎕SIGNAL⊂optÊ
      _←opts ⎕NS ⍺                                          ⍝ Add user options
  1≥≡⍵:FnOrFi,⍵                                             ⍝ If ⍵ is CV, see of a fn (fi:0) or a file (fi:1)?
      pos←0                                                 ⍝ pos:     Our position on this line.
      noCod←1                                               ⍝ noCod:   Just code on the line of ⍵?
      stI cdI _ cmI spI← ⍳≢pats← (
          '^'                                               ⍝ start    (of line)
          '''[^'']*''|[^⍝''\h]+'                            ⍝ code     (fragments)
          '(*F)' '^(\h*⍝[^⍝]*)\h{5,}(⍝.*)$'⊃⍨ opts.pairs    ⍝ double comments:  Nop unless opts.pairs.
          '\h*⍝.*$'                                         ⍝ comment  (w/ preceding spaces)
          '\h+'                                             ⍝ spaces   (not before comment)
      )
      pats ⎕R{
          m←⍵.Match
          Case←⍵.PatternNum∘=
        Case stI:m⊣pos⊢←0⊣noCod⊢←1                          ⍝ Start of line
        Case cdI:m⊣pos+←≢m⊣noCod⊢←0                         ⍝ Code found
        Case spI:m⊣pos+←≢m                                  ⍝ Spaces (not foll by comment)
      ⍝ Case cmI, cm2I ↓↓↓                                  ⍝ Comments (poss. preceded by spaces)
          asis←noCod∧opts.min>pos+nsp←+/∧\m=' '             ⍝ If comment is near start of line (<min), ...
        asis:{
          Case cmI: m                                       ⍝ ... keep leading spaces
        ⍝ (pairs: 1)?                                       ⍝ Pairs of comments handled here ↓↓↓                                      
            cm1 cm2←⍵.{ Lengths[⍵]↑ Offsets[⍵]↓ Block}¨ 1 2
            pos+← ≢cm1 
            m← cm1, opts.(tab inc)Align pos+1
            m, ' ', cm2 
        } ⍵                                             
          m←' ', nsp↓ m                                     ⍝ Not <min>. Guarantee 1 leading space
          m,⍨opts.(tab inc)Align pos+1                      ⍝ Align at "next" tab stop (per inc), if >tab already.
      }⊣⍵
}
